{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to flag something critical before we go any further. During my inspection this morning, the crane brake lining measured only 18% remaining. Our maintenance standard requires immediate removal from service when brake lining is below 20%. This isn't a Friday issue anymore — the crane needs to come out of service now. The repair itself is a 6-hour brake replacement, but after that we also have to perform a 125% rated-capacity proof-load test before the crane can return to service. I haven't entered this in the maintenance system yet, but I'm putting it on the table right now so we can plan around it."}
```

